(1800201, 242820, 24111, '<td valign="top">Good one Goodman!</td>', 'Good one Goodman!', '2005-10-21 00:59:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1800481, 242582, 45559, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by elee3009:</b></div><hr/><i> This is such a startling stare you''ve captured and for that alone, I think it works great as an image!  Very nice overall.  It probably scored low because viewers couldn''t understand how it represents Pride.  Maybe you could explain a little.  Altho'' voting is over, it''ll open up our minds a little as to how different people see pride. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>   First of all thanks for the comment.As I can see most of the photographers/users on this site are from the US.So far so good.A lot of photos in this challenge were about flags(the US flag) which it doesn''t inspires me pride, maybe because i''m european.The other category were children which is also some kind of photographers personal pride.It didn''t reflect a general view of the challenge(in my opinion).The photos are very well done but i don''t see more pride in a flag than in my girlfriend eye.But what''s done is done.<br/>   Now about my "EYE" ...i tried to expres in my shot the pride of a woman, because we all know that women,unlike man, are in a continnuous competition one with another.And there is a competition about everything:clothes,shues,parfumes,boyfriends/husbands etc.etc.</td>', 'Originally posted by elee3009: This is such a startling stare you''ve captured and for that alone, I think it works great as an image!  Very nice overall.  It probably scored low because viewers couldn''t understand how it represents Pride.  Maybe you could explain a little.  Altho'' voting is over, it''ll open up our minds a little as to how different people see pride. :)      First of all thanks for the comment.As I can see most of the photographers/users on this site are from the US.So far so good.A lot of photos in this challenge were about flags(the US flag) which it doesn''t inspires me pride, maybe because i''m european.The other category were children which is also some kind of photographers personal pride.It didn''t reflect a general view of the challenge(in my opinion).The photos are very well done but i don''t see more pride in a flag than in my girlfriend eye.But what''s done is done.   Now about my "EYE" ...i tried to expres in my shot the pride of a woman, because we all know that women,unlike man, are in a continnuous competition one with another.And there is a competition about everything:clothes,shues,parfumes,boyfriends/husbands etc.etc.', '2005-10-21 06:17:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1800702, 242267, 31889, '<td valign="top">Them are the breaks.<br/> <br/>I was reviewing the shots I''d taken over the past few days for a challenge entry and this was the one that I was most happy with.  It wasn''t until going though the verification steps that I realised I''d pp''ed some imperfections from under the nostrils and on the left cheek which is against the rules of the basic challenge.<br/> <br/>Needless to say it was a stupid thing to do.</td>', 'Them are the breaks. I was reviewing the shots I''d taken over the past few days for a challenge entry and this was the one that I was most happy with.  It wasn''t until going though the verification steps that I realised I''d pp''ed some imperfections from under the nostrils and on the left cheek which is against the rules of the basic challenge. Needless to say it was a stupid thing to do.', '2005-10-21 10:19:15.000000', NULL, 0),
